"Do you want to reject the key, trust temporarily, or trust always? [r/t/a/?] (r):\n"

#. type: Title =
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-taskomatic.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshooting Taskomatic"
msgstr "ການແກ້ໄຂບັນຫາ Taskomatic"

#
#
#
#. PUT THIS COMMENT AT THE TOP OF TROUBLESHOOTING SECTIONS
#. Troubleshooting format:
#. One sentence each:
#. Cause: What created the problem?
#. Consequence: What does the user see when this happens?
#. Fix: What can the user do to fix this problem?
#. Result: What happens after the user has completed the fix?
#. If more detailed instructions are required, put them in a "Resolving" procedure:
#. .Procedure: Resolving Widget Wobbles
#. . First step
#. . Another step
#. . Last step
#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-taskomatic.adoc:2
msgid ""
"Repository metadata regeneration is a relatively intensive process, so "
"Taskomatic can take several minutes to complete.  Additionally, if "
"Taskomatic crashes, repository metadata regeneration can be interrupted."
msgstr "ການສ້າງເມຕາດາຕາ (metadata) ຂອງຄັງເກັບໃໝ່ແມ່ນຂະບວນການທີ່ຂ້ອນຂ້າງໜັກ, ດັ່ງນັ້ນ Taskomatic ອາດຈະໃຊ້ເວລາຫຼາຍນາທີກວ່າຈະສຳເລັດ. ນອກຈາກນັ້ນ, ຖ້າ Taskomatic ເຮັດວຽກຜິດພາດ (crashes), ການສ້າງເມຕາດາຕາຂອງຄັງເກັບອາດຈະຖືກຂັດຈັງຫວະ."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-taskomatic.adoc:4
msgid ""
"If Taskomatic is still running, or if the process has crashed, package "
"updates can seem available in the {webui}, but do not appear on the client, "
"and attempts to update the client fail.  In this case, the `zypper ref` "
"command shows an error like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-taskomatic.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Valid metadata not found at specified URL\n"
msgstr "Valid metadata not found at specified URL\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-taskomatic.adoc:6
msgid ""
"To correct this, determine if Taskomatic is still in the process of "
"generating repository metadata, or if a crash could have occurred.  Wait for "
"metadata regeneration to complete or restart Taskomatic after a crash in "
"order for client updates to be carried out correctly."
msgstr "ເພື່ອແກ້ໄຂບັນຫານີ້, ໃຫ້ກວດເບິ່ງວ່າ Taskomatic ຍັງຢູ່ໃນຂະບວນການສ້າງເມຕາດາຕາຂອງຄັງເກັບຫຼືບໍ່, ຫຼື ມີການຜິດພາດເກີດຂຶ້ນ. ໃຫ້ລໍຖ້າຈົນກວ່າການສ້າງເມຕາດາຕາຈະສຳເລັດ ຫຼື ເລີ່ມ Taskomatic ໃໝ່ຫຼັງຈາກການຜິດພາດ ເພື່ອໃຫ້ການອັບເດດເຄື່ອງລູກຂ່າຍສາມາດດຳເນີນການໄດ້ຢ່າງຖືກຕ້ອງ."

#. type: Block title
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-taskomatic.adoc:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "Procedure: Resolving Taskomatic Problems"
msgstr "ຂັ້ນຕອນ: ການແກ້ໄຂບັນຫາ Taskomatic"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-taskomatic.adoc:8
msgid ""
"On the {productname} Server, check the "
"`/var/log/rhn/rhn_taskomatic_daemon.log` file to determine if any metadata "
"regeneration processes are still running, or if a crash occurred."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-taskomatic.adoc:9
msgid "Restart taskomatic:"
msgstr "ເລີ່ມ taskomatic ໃໝ່:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-taskomatic.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "service taskomatic restart\n"
msgstr "service taskomatic restart\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-taskomatic.adoc:11
msgid ""
"In the Taskomatic log files, you can identify the section related to "
"metadata regeneration by looking for opening and closing lines that look "
"like this:"
msgstr "ໃນໄຟລ໌ບັນທຶກຂອງ Taskomatic, ທ່ານສາມາດລະບຸພາກສ່ວນທີ່ກ່ຽວຂ້ອງກັບການສ້າງເມຕາດາຕາໄດ້ໂດຍການຊອກຫາແຖວເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ ແລະ ສິ້ນສຸດທີ່ເບິ່ງຄືປະມານນີ້:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-taskomatic.adoc:12
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<YYYY-DD-MM> <HH:MM:SS>,174 [Thread-584] INFO  "
"com.redhat.rhn.taskomatic.task.repomd.RepositoryWriter - Generating new "
"repository metadata for channel "
"'cloned-2018-q1-sles12-sp3-updates-x86_64'(sha256) 550 packages, 140 "
"errata\n"
msgstr "<YYYY-DD-MM> <HH:MM:SS>,174 [Thread-584] INFO  com.redhat.rhn.taskomatic.task.repomd.RepositoryWriter - Generating new repository metadata for channel 'cloned-2018-q1-sles12-sp3-updates-x86_64'(sha256) 550 packages, 140 errata\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-taskomatic.adoc:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "...\n"
msgstr "...\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-taskomatic.adoc:14
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<YYYY-DD-MM> <HH:MM:SS>,704 [Thread-584] INFO  "
"com.redhat.rhn.taskomatic.task.repomd.RepositoryWriter - Repository metadata "
"generation for 'cloned-2018-q1-sles12-sp3-updates-x86_64' finished in 4 "
"seconds\n"
msgstr "<YYYY-DD-MM> <HH:MM:SS>,704 [Thread-584] INFO  com.redhat.rhn.taskomatic.task.repomd.RepositoryWriter - Repository metadata generation for 'cloned-2018-q1-sles12-sp3-updates-x86_64' finished in 4 seconds\n"

#. type: Title =
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-webui-fails-load.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshooting {webui} Fails to Load"
msgstr "ການແກ້ໄຂບັນຫາ {webui} ບໍ່ສາມາດໂຫຼດໄດ້"

#
#
#
#
#
#. PUT THIS COMMENT AT THE TOP OF TROUBLESHOOTING SECTIONS
#. Troubleshooting format:
#. One sentence each:
#. Cause: What created the problem?
#. Consequence: What does the user see when this happens?
#. Fix: What can the user do to fix this problem?
#. Result: What happens after the user has completed the fix?
#. If more detailed instructions are required, put them in a "Resolving" procedure:
#. .Procedure: Resolving Widget Wobbles
#. . First step
#. . Another step
#. . Last step
#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-webui-fails-load.adoc:2
msgid ""
"Sometimes, the {webui} will not load after migration.  This is usually "
"caused by browser caching, if the new system has the same hostname and IP "
"address as the old system.  This duplication can confuse some browsers."
msgstr "ບາງຄັ້ງ, {webui} ຈະບໍ່ໂຫຼດຫຼັງຈາກການຍ້າຍລະບົບ (migration). ໂດຍປົກກະຕິແລ້ວແມ່ນເກີດຈາກແຄຊ໌ຂອງບຣາວເຊີ (browser caching), ຖ້າລະບົບໃໝ່ມີຊື່ໂຮສ ແລະ ທີ່ຢູ່ IP ດຽວກັນກັບລະບົບເກົ່າ. ການຊ້ຳຊ້ອນນີອາດຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ບຣາວເຊີບາງອັນສັບສົນ."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-webui-fails-load.adoc:3
msgid ""
"This issue is resolved by clearing the cache and reloading the page.  In "
"most browsers, you can do this quickly by pressing kbd:[Ctrl+F5]."
msgstr "ບັນຫານີ້ສາມາດແກ້ໄຂໄດ້ໂດຍການລ້າງແຄຊ໌ ແລະ ໂຫຼດໜ້າໃໝ່. ໃນບຣາວເຊີສ່ວນໃຫຍ່, ທ່ານສາມາດເຮັດສິ່ງນີ້ໄດ້ຢ່າງໄວວາໂດຍການກົດ kbd:[Ctrl+F5]."

#. type: Title =
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Replacing wicked with NetworkManager after Host OS Upgrade"
msgstr ""

#
#. Applies to: SUSE Multi-Linux Manager 5.0 / 5.1 on SL Micro 6.1
#. Platform: Microsoft Azure (cloud image deployments)
#. Cause: After upgrading the host OS from SLE Micro 5.5 to SL Micro 6.1, wicked remains active.
#. Consequence: Wicked packages become orphaned with no repository or security updates.
#. Fix: Install NetworkManager inside a transactional shell, remove wicked, enable NetworkManager, and reboot.
#. Result: NetworkManager manages the network and the system is in a supported configuration.
#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Problem description"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:3
msgid ""
"In some cases, after upgrading the {productname} host OS from SLE Micro 5.5 "
"to SL Micro 6.1, the system may continue running wicked as the active "
"network manager."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:4
msgid "This is an unsupported configuration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:5
msgid ""
"Wicked packages carried over from the previous installation become orphaned "
"as they are no longer available in any SL Micro 6.1 repository and receive "
"no security updates."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:6
msgid ""
"{productname} runs as a container on the SL Micro host.  Network management "
"is handled entirely by the host OS.  The {productname} container does not "
"require any changes during this procedure."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:7
msgid "The following symptoms confirm the system is affected:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:8
msgid "`systemctl status wicked` shows `active (exited)`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:9
msgid ""
"`systemctl status NetworkManager` shows `Unit NetworkManager.service could "
"not be found`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:10
msgid "`systemctl show -p Id network.service` returns `Id=wicked.service`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:11
msgid ""
"`sudo zypper se -s wicked` shows wicked listed under `(System Packages)` "
"with no repository"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:12
msgid ""
"This procedure applies to systems using DHCP, which is the standard "
"configuration for {productname} cloud images.  If your deployment uses "
"static IP addresses, VLANs, custom bonding, or other non-standard network "
"configurations, do not proceed.  Contact SUSE Support for guidance specific "
"to your configuration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "Scope and impact"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:14
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Item | Detail\n"
" \n"
"| Applies to\n"
"| {productname} 5.0 and 5.1 on SL Micro 6.1\n"
" \n"
"| Network interruption\n"
"| The system is briefly unreachable during the reboot at the end of this "
"procedure\n"
" \n"
"| {productname} container\n"
"| Remains running throughout.\n"
"No changes to the container are required.\n"
" \n"
"| IP address\n"
"| Unchanged after migration when using DHCP with a cloud provider.\n"
"DHCP leases are typically bound to the MAC address.\n"
" \n"
"| Minions\n"
"| No reconfiguration required.\n"
"Minions connect to the same IP address after the migration.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:16
msgid "Before starting:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:17
msgid ""
"Ensure you have out-of-band console access to the system (for example, the "
"serial console provided by your cloud platform or hypervisor).  This is your "
"recovery path if the network does not come back correctly after the reboot."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:18
msgid "Confirm the {productname} container is running and healthy:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:19
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:67
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo podman ps\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:20
msgid ""
"Record the current IP address and routing table on the host.  You will "
"verify these are unchanged after the migration:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:21
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"ip addr show eth0\n"
"ip route show\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "Migration procedure"
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:23
#, no-wrap
msgid "Procedure: Migrating wicked to NetworkManager"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block _
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:24
msgid ""
"Take a snapshot before making any changes.  This is your rollback point if "
"something goes wrong."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:25
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo snapper create -d \"Pre-NetworkManager-Migration\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:26
msgid ""
"Note the snapshot number from the output.  You will need it if you need to "
"roll back."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo snapper list\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:28
msgid "Open a transactional update shell to apply changes."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:29
msgid ""
"All changes made here are staged atomically and only take effect after the "
"reboot in the next step."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo transactional-update shell\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:31
msgid "Inside the shell, install NetworkManager:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:32
#, no-wrap
msgid "zypper in NetworkManager\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:33
msgid ""
"Confirm with `y` when prompted.  NetworkManager and its dependencies are "
"installed from the SL Micro-6.1 repositories."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:34
msgid "Remove the orphaned wicked packages:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:35
#, no-wrap
msgid "zypper rm wicked wicked-service cockpit-wicked\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:36
msgid "Confirm with `y` when prompted."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:37
msgid "During the wicked removal you will see warnings similar to the following:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:38
#, no-wrap
msgid " warning: file wicked: remove failed: No such file or directory\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:39
msgid ""
"These warnings are expected.  Some wicked files were already absent after "
"the OS upgrade.  The removal completes successfully.  Look for the following "
"lines to confirm the critical symlinks were removed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:40
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" Removed \"/etc/systemd/system/network.service\".\n"
" Removed \"/etc/systemd/system/multi-user.target.wants/wicked.service\".\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:41
msgid "Enable NetworkManager so it starts on the next boot:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "systemctl enable NetworkManager\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:43
msgid "You should see the following symlinks created:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:44
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" Created symlink /etc/systemd/system/network.service → "
"/usr/lib/systemd/system/NetworkManager.service.\n"
" Created symlink "
"/etc/systemd/system/multi-user.target.wants/NetworkManager.service → ...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:45
msgid "Exit the transactional shell:"
msgstr "ອອກຈາກ transactional shell:"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:47
msgid "Reboot."
msgstr "ຣີບູດ (Reboot)."

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:48
msgid ""
"The system will lose network connectivity during the reboot.  SSH sessions "
"will be terminated.  Use your out-of-band console to monitor the reboot if "
"needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:49
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo reboot\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:50
msgid ""
"Verify the migration after the system comes back up.  Run the following "
"checks on the host."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:51
msgid "Confirm `network.service` now points to NetworkManager:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:52
#, no-wrap
msgid "systemctl show -p Id network.service\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:53
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:57
msgid "Expected output:"
msgstr "ຜົນໄດ້ຮັບທີ່ຄາດຫວັງ:"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:54
#, no-wrap
msgid " Id=NetworkManager.service\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:55
msgid "Confirm wicked packages are fully removed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:56
#, no-wrap
msgid "rpm -q wicked wicked-service\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:58
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" package wicked is not installed\n"
" package wicked-service is not installed\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:59
msgid "Confirm the IP address is unchanged:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:60
#, no-wrap
msgid "ip addr show eth0\n"
msgstr ""

#.  For more information, see xref:tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc#ts-ip-changed[IP Address Changed After Reboot].
#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:61
msgid ""
"The IP address must match what was recorded before the migration.  If it has "
"changed, minions will lose connectivity to {productname}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:62
msgid "Confirm the routing table is intact:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:63
#, no-wrap
msgid "ip route show\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:64
msgid ""
"Compare the output against the routing table recorded before the migration "
"and verify all routes are present."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:65
msgid ""
"If any routes are missing immediately after boot, wait 90 seconds and check "
"again.  The `cloud-netconfig` service runs on a 60-second timer and restores "
"any missing cloud-provider-specific routes automatically."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:66
msgid "Confirm the {productname} container is running:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:68
msgid "The container should show status `healthy` within a few minutes of boot."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:69
#, no-wrap
msgid "The changes after the migration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/modules/administration/pages/troubleshooting/tshoot-wicked-to-networkmanager.adoc:70
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Item | Notes\n"
" \n"
"| IP address\n"
"| Unchanged when using DHCP.\n"
"NetworkManager obtains the same address via DHCP.\n"
" \n"
"| Slave or bonded interfaces\n"
"| Slave interfaces remain present and attached to their master.\n"
"They no longer appear in `ip addr show` because NetworkManager does not "
"display slave interfaces there.\n"
"Use `ip link show <interface>` to confirm they are present.\n"
"This is expected behaviour and has no impact on network performance.\n"
" \n"
"| Cloud-provider-specific routes\n"
"| Managed by `cloud-netconfig`, which operates independently of the network "
"manager and continues to do so after the switch.\n"
"Routes are restored within 60 seconds if missing after boot.\n"
" \n"
"| IPv6 link-local address\n"
"| The link-local address on the primary interface changes because "
"NetworkManager generates it differently from wicked.\n"
"This has no impact on standard {productname} deployments which use IPv4.\n"
" \n"
"| Default route metric\n"
"| NetworkManager adds an explicit `metric 100` to the default route.\n"
"This is correct behaviour and has no negative impact.\n"
" \n"
"| NetworkManager connection files\n"
"| NetworkManager auto-generates connection definitions in "
"`/var/run/NetworkManager/system-connections/` which is a tmpfs location.\n"
"These are regenerated on every boot from DHCP.\n"
"The original wicked configuration in `/etc/sysconfig/network/ifcfg-*` is "
"left in place but is not read by NetworkManager.\n"
" \n"
"| {productname} container\n"
"| Not affected.\n"
"Continues running without modification or restart.\n"
msgstr ""

